* tb1_op: operating point of lane 0 + bias of lvds_rx_x3 (task T2 part 2, PLAN_V2 TB1).  GENERATED by sim/tb1_op/make_deck.py -- do not edit.
* grid: vic (common mode), vid (differential input of lane 0).  EN = 1.  Lanes 1 and 2 sit at VIC with VID = 0.
* Hooks (hooks.py:post_tb1) compare every device with the sizing script / LUT and write the pass/fail metrics.
{header}
{seed_line}
* rshunt: 100 Gohm from every node to ground (7 nA at 3.6 V): without it floating nodes break ngspice's gmin/source stepping
.option rshunt=1e11
.param vidv = {vid}
.include {deck_dir}/../../sizing/sizes.spice
.param flag_nmos_pair = 0
.include {deck_dir}/../../netlist/lvds_rx_core.spice
Vsup vdd 0 {vdd}
Ben en 0 V=1*v(vdd)
Bcm cm 0 V={vic}*v(vdd)/{vdd}
Vp0 rx0_p cm dc {vidv/2}
Vn0 rx0_n cm dc {-vidv/2}
Vp1 rx1_p cm dc 0
Vn1 rx1_n cm dc 0
Vp2 rx2_p cm dc 0
Vn2 rx2_n cm dc 0
Xdut vdd 0 rx0_p rx0_n rx1_p rx1_n rx2_p rx2_n en rx0_o rx1_o rx2_o lvds_rx_x3
.control
* DC convergence: ramp the supply (EN and VIC scale with it) from 0.3 V to VDD; the last point is the operating point (plain `op` fails, see log/T2_report.md)
dc Vsup 0.3 {vdd} 0.1
let n = length(v(vdd)) - 1
let ivv = -i(Vsup)
let idd = ivv[n]
echo RESULT idd $&idd
let vds_xbias_xmen_p = abs(v(xdut.xbias.enb)[n] - v(vdd)[n])
let vgs_xbias_xmen_p = abs(v(en)[n] - v(vdd)[n])
let vsb_xbias_xmen_p = abs(v(vdd)[n] - v(vdd)[n])
